  "body": "Leonard,\n\nThe bridge send list is done. It's \"Q4 update - send list\" in my Q4 2025 investor update folder (shared with you), and it covers everything as of end of day Tue Sep 30 PT. Here's how many are in each group:\n\n- New investor: 0 firms, 1 angel (Anton Bernstein, $25K. His DocuSign Completed notice came in Sep 26.)\n- In talks: 8 firms, 1 angel (a16z, GFR Fund, Dentsu, T-Accelerate, NCsoft, SciPlay, Homa, Brightwater Games Fund, plus Paul Heydon at $50K. His SAFE is still unsigned in DocuSign, so he isn't a new investor yet.)\n- Awaiting reply: 14 firms, 0 angels\n- Keep warm: 2 firms, 0 angels (LVP and Hiro Capital). Both are now on a Keep warm checklist on the Existing Investor Update card.\n\nTotal: 24 firms and 2 angels.\n\nA few things to know before Monday:\n- Build access: only T-Accelerate and Dentsu are \"iOS only\". Arthur found on Sep 30 that the Play investor tester list was never attached to the internal track, even though ZOM-567 shows them as added. The other in-talks firms have no internal build access yet.\n- Off-list firms with a call on my calendar: Homa (Sep 18, bridge plus co-dev) and Brightwater (Sep 25).\n- Left off: Play Ventures (passed via Griffin), Grishin, 1AM/March, Lakestar and Iamgaming (all passed without a call). Mattel was RFP only. Kevin Lin, Mike Fischer and Demetri had no contact from us this round.\n- a16z is in talks. The speedrun rejection is the program's decision, not their answer on the bridge.\n\nTalk Monday.\n\nFred",
